WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.234
-Our next guest can be
seen at Zanies in Nashville

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:05.601
December 28th.

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:08.567
Please welcome
the very funny Jay Jurden!

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:11.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:18.701
-Hey, y'all.

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:20.767
I'm...pretty dumb.

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:21.834
Yeah.

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:23.701
No, don't let
this turtleneck fool you.

00:00:23.701 --> 00:00:25.701
I can come out here
and pretend like I know stuff,

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:27.934
but when I go home,
I'm definitely gonna be like,

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:32.701
"Oh, there's a 'U'
in 'camouflage'?"

00:00:32.701 --> 00:00:36.734
Doing a good job of hiding.
Like, that's...

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:40.534
Speaking of being dumb,
I recently got married!

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:42.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
Okay.

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:45.968
Alright. Yeah.
To a dude.

00:00:45.968 --> 00:00:48.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oh, okay.

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:52.033
Yeah! Alright!
I saw some people stop clapping.

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:56.467
Listen, I love homophobia.
It keeps me on my toes.

00:00:56.467 --> 00:01:00.200
Now, I know there are
some old-fashioned people here,

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.834
some people here
who believe marriage is

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:03.834
strictly between a man, a woman,

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:07.501
and eventually
a much younger woman.

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:11.601
A much younger woman who
happened to get

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:14.968
this executive-assistant
position with no experience.

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:18.901
All I'm saying is, I don't think
Tasha "knows Excel."

00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:20.901
[ Applause ]

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:27.701
Me and my husband --
we got married in New York City,

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:29.400
but we wanted to have
a traditional

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.701
Southern gay wedding.

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:35.000
So we had a cake.
We had a deejay.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.701
We had protesters.

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:41.300
And, y'all, they were
making some good points.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.400
One of the signs said,
"This is a choice."

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.767
I was like, "Of course
we have vegan options.

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:47.400
Come on, man."

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.734
Here's what they don't tell you.

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:51.234
When you get married
as a man to another man,

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:53.067
you spend most of
your wedding day

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:55.133
introducing gay men
who live in New York City

00:01:55.133 --> 00:02:00.167
to other gay men
they have already slept with.

00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:02.667
So most of my wedding day,
I was stuck saying stuff like,

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:06.200
"Well, Benjamin, you know Todd."

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:09.234
Shane, you know Todd."

00:02:09.234 --> 00:02:10.767
Michael, you know Todd.

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:13.200
Wait a second.
Does everyone know Todd?"

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.634
And then my husband was like,
"Jay, do you know Todd?"

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:19.667
And I was like, "Ooh!

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:20.801
I do."

00:02:20.801 --> 00:02:22.934
And then -- and then
I had to remind him.

00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:26.167
I said, "No, baby.
We know Todd."

00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:27.801
And he was like,
"Oh, that's Todd?

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:30.400
I didn't recognize him
standing up."

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:36.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:43.400
I'm surprised y'all
let me get away with that one.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.200
We had a fun officiant
at our wedding.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.868
Our wedding officiant, Dani,
with an "I," she was the best.

00:02:47.868 --> 00:02:49.767
She walked in.
She was like, "Hey, y'all.

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:53.534
We are gathered here today in
front of friends, family, God.

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:55.701
I'm kidding. He ain't watching.
Let's turn up."

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:58.834
And I was like, "Let's go!"

00:02:58.834 --> 00:03:01.734
Now, something interesting
just happened.

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:03.133
When I said
I was married to a dude,

00:03:03.133 --> 00:03:05.234
I heard a bunch of "whoos!"

00:03:05.234 --> 00:03:09.701
And that let me know it's a lot
of straight women here.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:12.167
Straight girls, I love y'all.
We go way back.

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:13.167
Middle school.

00:03:13.167 --> 00:03:15.033
Now...

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:17.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:24.767
Straight women,
are y'all doing okay?

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:26.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
Alright.

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:29.167
Then why y'all
love dating ugly dudes?

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:31.334
What is the reasoning?

00:03:31.334 --> 00:03:34.234
Do you know that being straight
doesn't have to be a dare?

00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:37.601
You can enjoy it?

00:03:37.601 --> 00:03:39.067
And then y'all come up to me
after the show

00:03:39.067 --> 00:03:41.067
and say stuff like,
"Well, Jay, just so you know,

00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:42.968
I happen to like
my men a little ugly.

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:45.100
Right, babe?"

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.167
And this poor guy is like,
"You hear that?

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:51.267
She only said 'a little.'"

00:03:51.267 --> 00:03:53.267
Y'all will brag to me
about your ugly man.

00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:54.601
You'll be like,
"Well, Jay, just so you know,

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:56.601
me and my ugly man --
we're flying to Paris."

00:03:56.601 --> 00:03:58.467
I'm like, "Yeah, he's got to get
back to Notre Dame.

00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:01.133
Those bells aren't gonna
ring themselves."

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.133
Of course,
I don't mean anyone here.

00:04:08.133 --> 00:04:09.701
Every straight guy here is a 10.

00:04:09.701 --> 00:04:12.501
If you don't believe me,
I'll kiss you on the way out.

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:15.567
That goes for you too, Jimmy.
I like the beard.

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:17.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:20.934 --> 00:04:22.801
But, seriously,
one of my friends --

00:04:22.801 --> 00:04:24.100
he's an old-school comedian.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:25.834
What's the word for that?
He's a misogynist.

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:27.801
And he said...

00:04:27.801 --> 00:04:30.000
He said, "Jay, these women
date these ugly men

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.434
just so they can
get their money."

00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:33.534
And I was like, "Yeah,
I know ugly men have money.

00:04:33.534 --> 00:04:36.467
I've been on a boat before."

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:39.267
Someone out there is like,
"Wait, I have a boat."

00:04:39.267 --> 00:04:42.334
I'm not talking about you.
You're gorgeous.

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:44.534
Seriously, do you think
the ugly community

00:04:44.534 --> 00:04:46.501
is going to cancel me
for that joke?

00:04:46.501 --> 00:04:48.767
Do you think the ugly community
is going to come for me?

00:04:48.767 --> 00:04:51.767
As long as they don't do it
in person. Yuck!

00:04:52.634 --> 00:04:55.534
No, everyone right now is so
obsessed with cancel culture.

00:04:55.534 --> 00:04:56.968
Everyone's worried about
cancel culture.

00:04:56.968 --> 00:04:59.868
Everyone except for me.

00:04:59.868 --> 00:05:06.501
Because do you understand how
hard it would be to cancel...

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:07.534
me?

00:05:07.534 --> 00:05:08.601
Come on, y'all.

00:05:08.601 --> 00:05:11.868
I'm black. I'm queer.
I'm left-handed.

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:13.267
There are...

00:05:13.267 --> 00:05:15.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:19.701 --> 00:05:21.801
...lots of words I can say.

00:05:21.801 --> 00:05:23.934
Alright, thank y'all so much.
I've been Jay Jurden.

00:05:23.934 --> 00:05:27.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:05:27.167 --> 00:05:29.234
-You're left-handed?
You're left-handed?

00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:31.601
-Yeah, I am.
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:31.601 --> 00:05:35.834
-Jay Jurden! Jay Jurden!
Come on!

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:37.868
He'll be at Zanies in Nashville.

00:05:37.868 --> 00:05:40.467
I love Zanies.
In Nashville December 28th.

00:05:40.467 --> 00:05:42.701
My thanks to Kevin Bacon,
Theo James,

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:46.434
Old 97's, Jay Jurden once again!

00:05:46.434 --> 00:05:47.968
He's left-handed, folks.

